config CHARY_BOND_REPAIR_ONCE
    bool
    default y if (SHIELD_CHARY_LEFT || SHIELD_CHARY_RIGHT || SHIELD_CHARY_DONGLE) && ZMK_BLE
    depends on SETTINGS && BT
    help
      Remove all legacy host and split Bluetooth bonds once, save a persistent
      migration marker, and reboot. Subsequent boots keep the newly established
      bonds normally.

config CHARY_FORCE_LEGACY_SPLIT_PAIRING
    bool
    default y if (SHIELD_CHARY_LEFT || SHIELD_CHARY_RIGHT || SHIELD_CHARY_DONGLE) && ZMK_BLE
    depends on BT && BT_SMP
    help
      Use BLE legacy Just Works pairing for the internal split link. This
      avoids the ECDH Secure Connections path, which stalls indefinitely on
      the affected dongle controller and ends in supervision timeout 0x08.
